<title>FRANCE: French sugar producers forecast lower '96 output.</title>
<headline>French sugar producers forecast lower '96 output.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>France may produce about four million tonnes of beet sugar in the 1996/97 season, down from 4.2 million in 1995/96, the French producers association SNFS predicted on Friday .</p>
<p>An SNFS spokeswoman said the forecast was based on data collected from beet processing plants up until this week.</p>
<p>She said SNFS expected to produce a new crop update within two to three weeks.</p>
<p>Beet harvesting began in France in late September.</p>
</text>
